  "facts": [
    {
      "text": "More than 5,900 exoplanets have been confirmed, and the NASA Exoplanet Archive updates that count continuously.",
      "source": "NASA Exoplanet Archive"
    },
    {
      "text": "The most common planet size in the known catalog has no Solar System analogue: worlds between Earth and Neptune in radius.",
      "source": "Kepler mission statistics"
    },
    {
      "text": "A radius gap near 1.8 Earth radii separates rocky super-Earths from gas-enveloped sub-Neptunes, most likely carved by atmospheric escape.",
      "source": "Fulton et al. radius-valley analyses"
    },
    {
      "text": "Equilibrium temperature assumes no atmosphere and no greenhouse effect. Earth's equilibrium temperature is about 255 K, roughly 33 K colder than its actual surface.",
      "source": "Standard planetary energy-balance model"
    },
    {
      "text": "Planets orbiting close to small, cool stars are expected to be tidally locked, with one hemisphere in permanent day.",
      "source": "Tidal evolution theory"
    },
    {
      "text": "Radial-velocity detections measure only a minimum mass, because the orbital inclination is usually unknown.",
      "source": "Radial velocity method"
    },
    {
      "text": "JWST detected sulphur dioxide on WASP-39 b, the first direct evidence of photochemistry in an exoplanet atmosphere.",
      "source": "JWST Transiting Exoplanet Early Release Science"
    },
    {
      "text": "The habitable zone is defined only as the orbital range where liquid water could be stable on a rocky surface. It says nothing about whether an atmosphere or water is actually present.",
      "source": "Habitable zone definition"
    },
    {
      "text": "TRAPPIST-1's seven planets are in a resonant chain: their orbital periods form near-integer ratios, a fossil record of migration during formation.",
      "source": "TRAPPIST-1 dynamical studies"
    },
    {
      "text": "No confirmed biosignature has ever been detected on any exoplanet.",
      "source": "Current scientific consensus"
    }
  ]
}
